$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method C: A mixture of 5-monosubstituted
triazole (4) (1 equiv), stannyl derivative (2) (1.3 equiv), PdCl2(PPh3)2
(0.02 equiv) and LiCl (3 equiv) or CuI (0.1 equiv) was irradiated at the
temperature and diring the appropriate time under Argon in a focused
microwave reactor DiscoverTM (CEM). The crude products 6a-c were purified
by flash chromatography on silica gel using a mixture of hexane:ethyl
acetate as the eluent.
2-(1-methyl-3-(thiophen-2-yl)-1H-1,2,4-triazol-5-yl)pyrazine 6c. Method
C. 2-(3-bromo-1-methyl-1H-1,2,4-triazol-5-yl)pyrazine 4g (70 mg, 0.3
mmol), tributyl(thiophen-2-yl)stannane 2a (145 mg, 0.39 mmol) and LiCl
were used. The crude was purified with a mixture of hexane:ethyl acetate
(6:1) as the eluent, 6c (61 mg, 83%) was obtained. mp: 139-140 °C. 1H-NMR
(CDCl3) δ 9.55 (d, J = 1.7 Hz, 1H, H-3 Py), 8.64-8.67 (m, 2H, H-5 and H-6
Py), 7.75 (dd, J = 3.7, 1.1 Hz, H-3 Thiop), 7.37 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.1 Hz,
1H, H-5 Thioph), 7.13 (dd, J = 5.1, 3.7 Hz, 1H, H-4 Thioph), 4.37 (s, 3H,
CH3). 13C-NMR (CDCl3) δ 157.5, 150.1, 145.4, 144.7, 143.5, 143.0, 133.5,
127.7, 126.5, 126.3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Stille reactions as a powerful tool for building
polyheteroaryl systems bearing a (1H)-1,2,4-triazole moiety
