$DATUM 2-Viny4-bromothiazole 21q as ustrated in FIG. 5. To a solution of 2,
4-dibromothiazole 20 (437 mg, 1.80 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in toluene was added
tri-n-butyl(vinyl)tin (552 mL, 1.89 mmol, 1.05 equiv) followed by
Pd(PPh3)4 (208 mg, 0.180 mmol, 0.1 equiv) and the resulting was heated at
100°C. After 21 h, the mixture was cooled and purified directly by flash
column chromatography (silica gel, 0® 9% ether in hexanes) to afford
2-viny4-bromothiazole 21q. Oil; Yield: (285 mg, 83%). Rf=0.50 (silica
gel, 17% ether in hexanes); IR (film) TTnlax 3121, 1470, 1259, 1226,
1124, 1082, 975, 926, 887, 833 cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) d 7.13 (s, 1
H, ArH), 6.86 (dd, J=17.5, 11.0 Hz, 1 H, CH =CH 2), 6.09 (d, J=17.5 Hz, 1
H, CHCH2), 5.59 (d, J=10.5 Hz, 1 H, CHCH2); 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, CDCl3) d
167.7, 129.5, 125.6, 120.8, 116.2; GC/MS (El), calcd for C5H4BrNS (M+)
189/191, found 189/191.
