$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
3-Chloro-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (11a). Typical Stille
procedure (Table X). To a stirred solution of
3-chloro-5-trifluoromethanesulfonoxy-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one (8) (65.0
mg, 0.22 mmol) in PhH (2 mL) at rt, was added
2-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (70 μL, 0.22 mmol) and Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (7.7 mg,
0.011 mmol) and the mixture was stirred at this temperature until no
starting material remained (TLC). The reaction mixture was then diluted
(DCM) and adsorbed onto silica. Chromatography (hexane/DCM, 7:3), gave
the title compound 11a. 3-Chloro-5-(thien-2-yl)-4H-1,2,6-thiadiazin-4-one
(11a), yield 83%. mp 123-124 °C (from cyclohexane), Rf 0.39 (hexane/DCM,
7:3); (found: C, 36.5; H, 1.2; N, 12.1. C7H3ClN2OS2 requires C, 36.4; H,
1.3; N, 12.1%); λmax(DCM)/nm 259 inf (log ε 2.82), 275 (2.93), 363
(3.29), 380 inf (3.21); νmax/cm-1 3125w, 3105w, 3092w and 3078w (Ar CH),
1657w, 1634s (C=O), 1543w, 1510w, 1481w, 1447w, 1420m, 1406m, 1369m,
1346w, 1298w, 1219m, 1182m, 1175m, 1128w, 1072w, 1053w, 1016m, 974w,
941w, 864m, 841m, 829m; δH(500 MHz; CDCl3) 8.29 (1H, dd, J 4.0, 1.0,
thienyl H), 7.69 (1H, dd, J 5.0, 1.0, thienyl H), 7.20 (1H, dd, J 4.8,
4.3, thienyl H); δC(125 MHz; CDCl3) 159.4 (s), 153.0 (s), 151.2 (s),
135.9 (s), 134.2 (d), 133.4 (d), 128.2 (d); m/z (EI) 232 (M++2, 38%), 230
(M+, 91), 141 (52), 123 (21), 121 (60), 109 (36), 95 (37), 93 (100), 71
(13), 64 (9), 58 (24).
