$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Stille Coupling Product 19. Protected 2-bromo
naphthohydroquinone 18 (389 mg, 0.80 mmol) was dissolved in toluene (8
mL) and stannane 2 (0.36 g, 0.92 mmol), tetrakis (triphenylphosphine)
palladium (0) (46 mg, 0.04 mmol) and a few crystals of
2,6-di-tert-butyl-4-methyl phenol (radical scavenger) were added. The
reaction mixture was stirred at reflux for 8 h, cooled and filtered
through Celite®. The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure.
The residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel with ethyl
acetate / hexane (1:30) to give a cis/trans-mixture of Stille coupling
product 19 (cis / trans 1:2) as a yellow oil (343 mg, 83 %). IR (neat) ν
2955, 2879, 1743, 1594, 1393, 1264, 1070, 742 cm-1; 1H-NMR (CD2Cl2) δ
7.63 and 7.61 (each dd, total 1H, each 3 J = 8.5 Hz, 4 J = 1.0 Hz,
aromatic proton, cis / trans 1:2 in the order given), 7.33 and 7.32 (each
t, total 1H, each 3 J = 8.5 Hz, C7H, cis / trans 1:2 in the order given),
6.89 (dt, 0.66H, 3 J = 16.0 Hz, 4 J = 1.4 Hz, C9H, trans isomer), 6.88
and 6.64 (each s, total 1H, C3H, trans / cis 2:1 in the order given),
6.83- 6.72 (m, 1.3H, aromatic proton and C9H cis-isomer), 6.18 and 5.92
(each dt, total 1H, 3 J = 16.0 Hz, 7.2 Hz and 3 J = 11.4 Hz, 7.4 Hz
respectively, C10H, trans / cis 2:1 in the order given), 3.89 and 3.87
(each s, total 3H, OMe, cis / trans 1:2 in the order given), 3.71 and
3.68 (each s, total 3H, OMe, trans / cis 2:1 in the order given), 3.34-
3.26 (m, 2H, C(11)H2), 1.20-0.68 (m, 30 H) ppm; 13C-NMR (CD2Cl2) δ
172.52, 172.33, 157.66, 147.28, 146.65, 144.16, 143.62, 132.18, 131.89,
123.65, 123.44, 120.46 and 120.29 (quart. C); 129.60, 129.36, 126.25,
126.19, 124.62, 122.37, 116.67, 116.07, 115.83, 112.64, 106.30 and 106.13
(CH); 39.04, 34.72, 6.09, 5.99, 5.59 and 5.55 (CH2); 55.84, 52.28, 52.24,
7.10, 7.05 and 7.03 (CH3) ppm; LRFAB: m/z = 516 (calc. for C28H44O5Si2:
516).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 67:33 trans:cis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Electrocyclic ring closure of the enols of vinyl quinones. A 2H-chromene
synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Parker, Kathlyn A.; Mindt, Thomas L.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2001), 3(24), 3875-3878

