$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Preparation of 3r (general procedure for
Stille coupling to afford 3a-c, 3g, 3h and 3r). To a two-necked flask
fitted with a suba-sealed condenser was added copper(I) iodide (0.021g,
0.11 mmol), triphenylphosphine (0.055 g, 0.21 mmol) and
tris-(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0)-chloroform complex (0.027 g,
0.052 mmol Pd). The flask was pump-purged twice with argon, then
thoroughly degassed, dry DMF (5 ml) added, followed by
[3-iodo-Z-prop-2-enyl](benzyloxy)acetate (0.267 g, 0.81 mmol in DMF (3
ml). The mixture was heated to 50°C under argon, then 1b (0.519g, 1.11
mmol in DMF (3 ml) was added in one portion. The mixture was heated at
50-65°C for 16 hours. Diethyl ether (10ml) was added followed by water
(50 ml). Extractive work-up, concentration in vacuo and column
chromatography (20% Et2O in petroleum ether, then 10% EtOAc in petroleum
ether).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM other coupling methods gave lower yields
