$DATUM 2,6-Bis(5’-dodecyl-2’-thienyl)cyclopentabithiophene-4-one (3) The
solution of 2,6-dibromo-cyclopenta[2,1-b:3,4-b’]-dithiophene-4-one3 (1,
0.35 g, 1 mmol) and 5-dodecyl-2-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (2, 1.35 g,
2.60 mmol) in toluene/DMF (6/1, v/v, 25 mL) was purged with N2 for 30
min, and Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (21.0 mg, 0.03 mmol) was then added. The reaction
mixture was heated to 110 °C for 36 h. Excess solvent was removed under
vacuum and the crude product was purified by column chromatography using
hexane-chloroform (3 : 1) as eluent to give 3. (0.56 g) in an 82% yield.
1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm = 7.00-6.97 (m, 4H), 6.69 (d, J = 3.3 Hz,
2H), 2.79 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 4H), 1.69 (m, 4H), 1.40-1.10 (m, 36H), 0.88 (m,
6H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ ppm = 146.71, 146.29, 142.03, 140.78,
133.85, 124.81, 123.56, 122.87, 117.0, 31.87, 31.47, 30.15, 29.63, 29.59,
29.57, 29.53, 29.47, 29.27, 29.03, 22.60, 13.93. EI MS: m/z = 692.1
([M+]), calculated exact mass for C41H56OS4: 692.3. Elemental analysis:
calculated for C41H56OS4, C71.04, H 8.14, O, 2.31, S 18.50, found:
C70.82, H 8.20.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
