$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(pyridin-2-yl)-4-(trifluoromethyl)quinoline (16a): To an oven dried 25
mL round bottomed flask with a stirbar was weighed the aryl bromide 10
(1348 mg, 0.50 mmol, 1.07 equiv.), Pd(Ph3P)2Cl2 (16.1 mg, 0.023 mmol,
0.05 equiv.), and Ph3P (12.3 mg, 0.047 mmol, 0.10 equiv.). Dry toluene
was charged to the flask and the solution was sparged with N2 for 20 min.
The pyridyl stannane 17a (173.0 mg, 0.47 mmol, 1 equiv.) was charged to
the flask by syringe. A water cooled condenser was attached to the flask
and the reaction mixture was heated to reflux overnight. After 16 h, the
reaction was cooled to room temperature and transferred to a separatory
funnel with CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The organic mixture was washed with saturated
NaHCO3 (1 × 30 mL) solution, which was subsequently back extracted with
CH2Cl2 (2 × 20 mL). The combined organics were dried over Na2SO4,
filtered and concentrated in vacuo. Purified by flash chromatography
eluting with hexanes containing 10% ethyl acetate and 1% triethyl amine
to provide the product 16a as a slightly yellow solid (105.9 mg, 0.386
mmol) in 82% yield. Rf = 0.25 (10% ethyl acetate, 1% triethyl amine in
hexanes) UV M.P.: 74-75 °C 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.39 (dd, J= 4.7,
4.7 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (dd, J= 7.4, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 7.82 (dd, J= 7.4, 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.88(dd, J= 7.4, 7.8 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.27 (d, J=
8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.67 (d, J= 8.2 Hz, 1H), 8.76 (d, J= 5.1 Hz, 1H), 8.94 (s,
1H) 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 116.5 (q, J= 5 Hz), 121.9, 122.1, 124.2
(q, J= 2 Hz), 124.4 (q, J= 198 Hz), 124.8, 128.5, 130.4, 130.9, 135.2 (q,
J= 32 Hz), 137.3, 148.8, 149.5, 155.2, 155.8. IR (neat): 3097 (w), 3067
(w), 3009 (w), 1610 (w), 1590 (m), 1555 (m), 1373 (s) cm-1 . HRMS: m/z
(ESI/TOF MS E+) Calculated[MH+] 275.0791, observed 275.0777.
