$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of Vinyl Amide 9 To a solution of compound 8 (0.500g, 0.110
mmol) in 20mL of DMF, tributyl(vinyl)tin (0.38mL, 0.140mmol), Pd2(dba)3
(100mg, 0.011 mmol) mmol) and AsPh3 (0.270 g, 0.088 mmol) were added. The
solution was stirred for 12 h at 50°C under an N2 atmosphere. After
cooling to rt, the reaction mixture was quenched with saturated NH4Cl
solution and extracted with ethyl acetate (20 mL x 3). The organic layer
was washed with water (10 ml x 3), dried over MgSO4 , and concentrated
after filtration. The crude product was purified by silica-gel column
chromatography (hexane-EA = 1:1) to afford compound 9 (0.340 g, 82%). 9,
yield 0.340 g, 82%. MS m/z =355 (M+); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400MHz) δ 8.05 (br
s, 1H), 7.71 (d, 1H, J = 8.0Hz), 7.16 (dd, 1H, J = 8.0Hz, J = 8.0Hz),
7.03-6.94 (m, 2H), 7.01 (s, 1H), 6.69 (s, 1H), 5.92 (s, 2H), 5.54 (d, 1H,
J = 16.8 Hz), 5.22 (d, 1H, J = 1 1.2 Hz), 3.87 (s, 3H), 3.75 (s, 3H),
3.62 (bt, 2H), 2.96 (t, 2H, J = 7.6 Hz); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
165.0, 152.3, 147.3, 146.5, 133.4, 130.3, 130.2, 126.4, 124.0, 122.5,
115.1, 114.0, 109.5, 105.3, 100.8, 60.9, 55.8, 40.5, 32.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
