$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4e To a solution of halide (8.940 mmol, 2.575
g) and corresponding organotin compound (9.830 mmol, 3.708 g) in DMF (27
ml) a portion of Pd black powder (0.18 mmol, 0.019 g) was suspended.
After 110 minutes of heating the reaction was worked-up. The suspension
was filtered to separating funnel containing EtOAc (200 mL) and saturated
solution of NH4Cl (100 mL) and extracted. The organic layer was then
extracted twice with 4% sol. of NaF (2×150 mL) and the precipitate was
filtered. The resulting solution was dried over Na2SO4. The crude mixture
was purified by column chromatography (gradient elution, hexanes:EtOAc
(8:2) → hexanes:EtOAc (6:4)) . The resulting solid was dissolved in the
smallest possible amount of hot EtOAc, then approx. four times larger
volume of hexanes was added and the solution was left in the freezer
overnight. Resulting white crystalline solid was collected and dried.
LiCl addition: Identical conditions were applied, except that 3 eq. of
LiCl were added to the mixture before it was heated (see Table 3 in the
text). The yield was remarkably higher (79 %), the reaction time dropped
down to 120 minutes. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6) δ 7.42-7.35 (m, 2H),
6.92-6.84 (m, 2H), 5.81 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 4.73-4.64 (m, 2H), 4.29 (d,
J = 5.3 Hz, 2H), 4.23-4.16 (m, 2H), 3.74 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz,
DMSO-d6) δ 158.48, 138.71, 133.51, 129.56, 127.38, 113.71, 58.11, 57.83,
55.21; IR (ATR) ν max 834, 999, 1029, 1050, 1187, 1247, 1292, 1513, 1631,
2957, 3034, 3284 cm-1; LRMS (APCI): m/z (rel. intensity) 177.1 [M-17]+
(100), 159.0 (93), 144.0 (39); HRMS (TOF-ESI+) m/z calcd for C11H14O3Na+
217.0841, found 217.0840.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Migita-Still coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Fully Substituted Pyranones via Quasi-Heterogeneous Genuinely Ligand-Free
Migita-Stille Coupling of Iodoacrylates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
