$DATUM 4,8-di(2-thienyl)-benzo[1,2-c;4,5-c′]bis[1,2,5]thiadiazole
(4,8-di(2-thienyl)-BBT) (2). 1.2 g of 4,8-dibromo-BBT (3.4 mmol), 239 mg
of Pd[PPh3]2Cl2 (10 mol % ) and 40 mL of anhydrous dioxane was added into
a round bottom flask charged with nitrogen. 2.7 mL of
2-(tributylstannyl)thiophene (8.5 mmol) was added and the reaction
mixture was refluxed for 24 hours under nitrogen. Another 1.6 mL of the
tin compound (5.1 mmol) was added and the reaction was continued for
another 24 hours. The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to room
temperature and 200 mL of methanol was added. The resulting solids were
colected by filtration, and washed repeatedly with methanol. Column
chromatography was carried out on silica using hexane:dichloromethane
(1:1) to yield 2 as dark blue crystals (1.00 g, 82 % yield). 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ, [ppm] 7.35 (t, 2 H, J = 4.4 Hz), 7.71 (d, 2 H, J = 5.2 Hz),
9.03 (d, 2 H, J = 4.0 Hz). Decomposition point: 316 °C. Anal. Calcd for
C14H6N4S4: C, 46.91; H, 1.69; N, 15.63; S, 35.78. Found: C, 46.78; H,
1.83; N, 15.44; S, 35.59. MALDI-TOF-MS m/z: 358.0 (M+); Mw calcd. for
C14H6N4S4 = 358.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot Synthesis of 4,8-Dibromobenzo[1,2-c;4,5-c']bis[1,2,5]thiadiazole
