$DATUM 71-43-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Cross-Coupling Procedures. Stille: The stannane 1c (1 equiv), the
halide (1 equiv), and the catalyst (0.05 equiv) were dissolved in benzene
or toluene and heated in a CEM Explorer PLS microwave unit under
nitrogen. The temperature in all microwave experiments was measured with
an external IR sensor. Alternatively, in the case of iodobenzene,
refluxing overnight gave similar results. 2-Chloro-5-phenylthiazole (2a):
22 Compound 2a was prepared according to the general Stille procedure.
Reaction parameters: 20 min; 175 °C; Pd(PPh3)4; benzene. Yield: 82% (79
mg, 0.40 mmol) colorless solid; mp 40-42 °C.1H NMR (CDCl3, 200 MHz): δ
7.34-7.55 (m, 5H), 7.71 (s, 1H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 50 MHz): δ 126.6 (d),
128.9 (d), 129.2 (d), 130.4 (s), 136.5 (d), 141.4 (s), 150.3 (s). MS (EI)
m/z (relative intensity): 197.09 (33), 195.07 (100), 160.11 (24), 134.03
(76), 89.07 (18).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenated 2'-Chlorobithiazoles via Pd-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling
Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stanetty, Peter; Schnuerch, Michael; Mihovilovic, Marko D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(10), 3754-3761

