$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,5-Dioctyloxy-2,6-di(2-thienyl)-9,10-anthraquinone (11) The
diiodoanthraquinone 1 (0.716 g, 1 mmol), 2-(tributylstannyl) thiophene
(4; 0.820 g, 2.20 mmol) and the catalyst, Pd(PPh3)4 (0.127 g, 0.11 mmol),
were dissolved in anhyd toluene (25 mL) under N2. The mixture was
refluxed for 4 d. After cooling to r.t., the solvent was distilled at
reduced pressure and the crude product was purified by column
chromatography over silica gel using PE-EtOAc (9:1) as the eluent to give
a product. Red solid, yield 0.508 g, 81%. mp 113-115 °C (EtOH-H2O, 8:2).
FTIR (KBr): 2950, 2920, 2850, 1680, 1480, 1460, 1390, 1290, 1260, 1240,
1210, 1040, 819, 693 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.90 (t, J = 6.2
Hz, 6 H), 1.27- 1.38 (m, 16 H), 1.30-1.54 (m, 4 H), 1.80 (quint, J = 6.2
Hz, 4 H), 4.07 (t, J = 6.2 Hz, 4 H), 7.03 (dd, J = 5.1, 3.6 Hz, 2 H),
7.05-7.09 (m, 2 H), 7.11 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H), 7.32 (dd, J = 5.1, 1.1 Hz,
2 H), 7.55 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2 H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.3,
22.8, 26.0, 29.2, 29.4, 29.5, 32.0, 69.4, 116.4, 124.8, 125.4, 125.6,
127.1, 127.2, 137.2, 137.3, 141.2, 151.2, 185.0. Anal Calcd for
C38H44O4S2: C, 72.57; H, 7.05; S, 10.20. Found: C, 72.61; H, 6.98; S,
10.16.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
