$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure for the synthesis of
5,6,11,12-tetrachalcogenophen-2-yl)tetracene Procedure for the synthesis
of 5,6,11,12-tetrachalcogenophen-2-yl)tetracene
5,6,11,12-Tetrachlorotetracene (Cl4-Tet) (0.363 g, 1.00 mmol),
tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0) (75%, 0.092 g, 0.075 mmol), and
cesium Fluoride (1.67 g, 11.0 mmol) were added to a two-neck flask
equipped with stir bar and it was then capped with a septum. The flask
was evacuated and then refilled with argon. Dioxane (3 ml) was added by
syringe, followed by addition of tri-tert-butylphosphine (0.061 g, 0.30
mmol) in dioxane (3 ml). The 2-tributylstannylchalcogenophene (5.0 mmol)
in dioxane (0.5 ml) was added by syringe, and the reaction mixture was
stirred at 100 °C for 2 days. After cooling, the reaction mixture was
evaporated and the residue was dissolved in chloroform. The solution was
filtered and the solvent was removed in vacuo. The residue was purified
by column chromatography on a silica gel using hexane/dichloromethane
mixture (2:1) as eluent to give pure product. The product was further
purified by recrystallization from dichloromethane layered with methanol.
Compound 2 (TR1): red crystals. 81%. Mp: 266-271 °C. Decomposition (5%
weight loss) temperature: 345 °C. 1H-NMR: δ/ppm (500 MHz, CDCl3, Me4Si) =
7.77 (d, 4H, J = 7.0 Hz); 7.24 (dd, 4H, J = 3.2 Hz, J = 7.0 Hz); 6.57 (d,
4H, J = 2.7 Hz); 6.47 (br, 4H); 2.49 (s, 12H). 13C-NMR: δ/ppm (125 MHz,
CDCl3) = 3113, 3058, 140.0, 132.3, 129.9, 129.8, 126.6, 125.9, 125.1,
15.4. MS/FD: m/z 612 (M+, 100%). IR: νmax/cm-1 = 3071, 2916, 1488, 1455,
1384, 1311, 1221, 1165, 1119, 1097, 1074, 1040, 970, 940, 892, 872, 854,
816, 795, 789, 759, 735, 712, 692, 679, 657. Anal. Calcd. For C38H28S4:
C, 74.47; H, 4.60; S, 20.93. Found: C, 74.14; H, 4.47; S, 20.74.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
