$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of 3,3-Diarylacrylonitriles :
General Procedure for the Synthesis of 3,3-Diarylacrylonitriles by the
Stille Cross-Coupling Reaction of
3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)acrylonitrile with Aromatic
Iodides or Bromides. A mixture of
(Z)-3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)acrylonitrile or
(E)-3-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(tributylstannyl)-acrylonitrile, (0.1 mmol,
1.0 equiv), aryl halide (1.20 equiv), cesium fluoride (2.20 equiv), and
Pd(dppf) (5.0 mol %) or Pd2(dba)3 (2.5 mol%) and PtBu3 (5.0 mol%) in
anhydrous DMF (1.0 mL, degassed by freeze-pump-thaw-pump method) was
stirred in dark under argon at 60 °C for indicated time. The reaction
mixture was then cooled to room temperature and filtered a short column
of silica gel (5 g), and the column was washed with ethyl acetate. The
organic solution was concentrated on arotary evaporator under vacuum. The
solvent was removed under reduced pressure and purified by column
chromatography on SiO2 eluting with EtOAc-hexanes. The crude residue was
purified by column chromatography on SiO2 eluting with hexane-EtOAc (4:1)
to afford
(Z)-3-(3,4-Dimethoxyphenyl)-3-(3,5-dimethylphenyl)acrylonitrile, yellow
oil, yield 74 mg, 81%. IR (film) 2209, 1600, 1515, 1463, 1260, 1137,
1024, 749 cm-1; EIMS m/z 293 (M+, 100), 278 (10); 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 7.08 (bs, 1 H), 7.03 (dd, J = 2.0, 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 6.99 (d, J = 2.0 Hz, 1
H), 6.92 (bs, 2 H), 6.91 (d, J = 8.2 Hz, 1 H), 5.58 (s, 1 H), 3.94 (s,
3H), 3.87 (s, 3 H), 2.31 (s, 6 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.4,
150.6, 148.7, 139.5, 38.3, 132.2, 129.8, 126.7, 123.3, 118.7, 112.8,
110.8, 93.3, 56.2, 56.1, 21.4; Anal. Calcd for C19H19NO2: C, 77.79; H,
6.53; N, 4.77. Found: C, 77.59; H, 6.54; N, 4.76.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, optimization study (optimized on catalysts), Stille reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Stereoselective Synthesis of 3,3-Diarylacrylonitriles as Tubulin
Polymerization Inhibitors
