$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A mixture of 6.34 g of III [3], 6.56 g of
hexamethyldistannane, 2.52 g of anhydrous lithium chloride, and 1.20 g of
tetrakis(triphenyl-phosphine)palladium in 75 mL of anhydrous dioxane was
heated with stirring for 1.5 h under argon.
tert-Butyl-4-(p-tolyl)-3,6-dihydro-2H-pyridine-1-carboxylate (IX) was
prepared by procedure [3]. Yield 81%, pale yellow substance. IR spectrum,
ν, cm-1: 1687 (C═O), 1618 (C═C). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.49 s (9H,
CMe3), 2.34 s (3H, CH3), 2.50-2.54 m (2H, CH2), 3.49-3.54 m (2H, NCH2),
4.06 d (2H, NCH2, J 7.6 Hz), 6.00-6.04 m (1H, CH═C), 7.18 d (2H, C6H2, J
8.2 Hz), 7.30 d (2H, C6H2, J 8.2 Hz). Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %):
274.48 (100) [M + H]+. Found, %: C 74.61; H 8.34; N 5.06. C17H23NO2.
Calculated, %: C 74.73; H 8.42; N 5.13. M 273.74.
