$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille Reaction; General Method. A mixture of
triazole (1.0 mmol), vinylstannane (1.2 mmol), and PdCl2(MeCN)2 (0.06
mmol) in DMF (2 mL) was stirred overnight at 40 °C under an argon
atmosphere for 12 h. The mixture was poured into EtOAc (10 mL), filtered,
washed with sat. NH4Cl (3 × 10 mL) and brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (10% w/w anhyd K2CO3-silica gel, pentane-EtOAc,
100:0 to 60:40). 1-Benzyl-5-vinyl-1H-1,2,3-triazole-4-carbaldehyde (5d).
Yellow solid; yield: 173 mg (81%). Reactant: Vinylstannane 4b. mp 50-51
°C. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 5.65 (s, 2 H), 5.82 (dd, J = 11.3, 1.4
Hz, 1 H), 6.59 (dd, J = 17.6, 1.4 Hz, 1 H), 6.72 (dd, J = 17.6, 11.3 Hz,
1 H), 7.17 (m, 2 H), 7.26-7.37 (m, 3 H), 10.19 (s, 1 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 52.0, 119.0, 126.7, 127.2, 128.4, 128.9, 133.8, 143.7, 185.1.
HRMS (ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C12H12N3O: 214.0975; found: 214.0972;
m/z [M + Na]+ calcd for C12H11N3NaO: 236.0794; found: 236.0791.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium-catalyzed cross-coupling of 1,4-disubstituted
5-iodo-1,2,3-triazoles with organotin reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Carcenac, Yvan; David-Quillot, Franck; Abarbri, Mohamed; Duchene, Alain;
Thibonnet, Jerome
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2013), 45(5), 633-638

