$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General coupling procedure The mixture of
bromosubstituted heteroarene (0.5 mmol), PdCl3(PPh3)2 (0.025 mmol) and
ferrocenylstannane 2 or 5 (0.55 mmol) in dry DMF (4 ml) was stirred at
120-130 °C for the time given in the Table. After the mixture was cooled
to room temperature, water (8 ml) was added and the resulting solution
was extracted with ether or dichloromethane. The organic layer was
sequentially washed with saturated KF solution and water, dried over
MgSO4, and evaporated the solvent to gave a residue which was purified by
chromatography on silica gel column (eluant: petroleum/acetone in the
ratio, which was determined by the TLC studies of each product). 3b,
yield 81%. 1H NMR(CDCl3), 2.26(S, 6H), 3.17(d, 1H, J = 12.7), 3.68(d. 1H,
J=12.7), 4.10(s, SH), 4.47(m, 2H), 4.72(m, 1H), 8.19(d, 1H, J = 8.42),
8.48(dd, 1H, J = 8.42, J = 2.11), 9.04(d, 1H, J = 2.11); IR(KBr) 3098,
3032, 1576, 1531. 1104, 10 18; MS(EI), 365(M+, 100), 321(M-44, 35.86),
58(44.84).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 1,2-disubstituted ferrocene containing a heteroaryl group
