$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Cross-Coupling Procedures. Stille: The
stannane 1c (1 equiv), the halide (1 equiv), and the catalyst (0.05
equiv) were dissolved in benzene or toluene and heated in a CEM Explorer
PLS microwave unit under nitrogen. The temperature in all microwave
experiments was measured with an external IR sensor. Alternatively, in
the case of iodobenzene, refluxing overnight gave similar results.
4-Bromo-2'-chloro-2,5'-bithiazole (10): Compound 10 was prepared
according to the general Stille procedure. Reaction parameters:
overnight, reflux, Pd(PPh3)4, benzene (thermal) or 20 min, 170 °C,
Pd(PPh3)4, benzene (microwave). Yield: 81% (112 mg, 0.40 mmol) yellow
solid. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 200 MHz): δ 7.23 (s, 1H), 7.93 (s, 1H). 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 50 MHz): δ 116.8 (d), 126.3 (s), 133.7 (s), 139.8 (d), 154.0 (s),
158.2 (s). MS (EI) m/z (relative intensity): 282.0 (100), 280.0 (67),
137.6 (48), 135.6 (46), 56.6 (52). Anal. Calcd for C6H2BrClN2S2: C,
25.59; H, 0.72; N, 9.95. Found: C, 25.82; H, 1.00; N, 9.87.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, regioselective, Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Halogenated 2'-Chlorobithiazoles via Pd-Catalyzed Cross-Coupling
Reactions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Stanetty, Peter; Schnuerch, Michael; Mihovilovic, Marko D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(10), 3754-3761

