$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for the sequence alkylation-Stille on
5-iodopyrid-2(1H)-one A1 (Method A1E): A mixture of A1 (1.0 mmol), the
corresponding alkyl halide (1.0 mmol) and K2CO3 (1.0 mmol) in toluene
(2.5 mL) was heated (110 °C) under argon until the starting material (A1)
had been consumed. After cooling, bis(triphenylphosphine)Palladium (II)
dichloride (0.10 mmol) and the corresponding stannane (1.1 mmol) were
added and heated under reflux under argon for 3-8 h. The mixture was
allowed to cool to room temperature, filtered through a pad of Celite,
washed (AcOEt, 3 times) and the filtrate was evaporated to dryness to
give a oily residue that was poured in water. After extraction with
dichloromethane, the organic phase was dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated
under reduced pressure. The residue was purified by column chromatography
(silica gel). A1B2E1: Purified by column chromatography on silica gel
using AcOEt/hexane (1:1) as eluent to afford 80% of a yellow oil. IR
(KBr): νmax/cm-1 1662. 1H-NMR (CDCl3 75 MHz), δ (ppm): 7.45 (dd, J= 9.5,
J= 2.4, Hz, 1H), 7.19 (d, J= 2.4 Hz, 1H), 6.54 (d, J= 9.5 Hz, 1H), 6.38
(dd, J= 6.6 Hz, J= 10.9 Hz, 1H), 5.42 (d, J= 17.4 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (d, J=
10.9 Hz, 1H), 3.94 (q, J= 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.32 (t, J= 7.2 Hz, 3H). 13C-NMR
(CDCl3 300 MHz), δ (ppm): 162.3, 136.3, 135.8, 131.9, 121.4, 117.8,
111.9, 45.2, 15.0. MS (70 eV) m/z (%): 149 (M+, 100), 121 (54).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
