$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4-(1-Dimethylsulfamoyl-4-(3-hydroxy-2-propenyl)imidazol-4-yl)-1-dimethylsulfamoyl-5-(2-propen-3-ol)imidazole
(22): N2 was bubbled through solution of 17 (2.43 g, 5.15 mmol) and
stannane 20 (4.90 g, 7.73 mmol) in dry DMF (100 ml). PPh3 (270 mg, 1.03
mmol), CuI (196 mg, 1.03 mmol) and Pd2(dba)3 (236 mg, 0.26 mmol) were
added and bubbling of N2 was continued for additional 2 min. The reaction
mixture was heated at 55 °C for 3 min. followed by addition of CsF (1.96
g, 12.9 mmol) and heating was continued for additional 1 h.3 The reaction
mixture was cooled to rt and a solution of TBAF (1M in THF, 12.87 ml,
12.87 mmol) was added. The reaction was stirred at rt for 5 h. Then the
DMF was removed by distillation under vaccum. Water (50 ml) and EtOAc
(100ml) were added to the residue, which was stirred vigorously and then
the mixture was filtered through bed of Celite. The filtrate was
partitioned and the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc. The organic
extracts were combined, dried (Na2SO4), concentrated and the residue was
purified by flash chromatography (EtOAc→EtOAc/methanol, 85:15) to give
product 22 (1.89 g, 80%) as a yellowish solid;
4-(1-Dimethylsulfamoyl-4-(3-hydroxy-2-propenyl)imidazol-4-yl)-1-dimethylsulfamoyl-5-(2-propen-3-ol)imidazole
(22), Yield 1.89 g (80%) m.p. 135-139 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz): δ = 7.90 (s,
1H), 7.89 (d, J = 1.4 Hz 1H), 7.04 (d, J = 1.4 Hz 1H), 6.60 (dt, J = 1.7,
16.1 Hz, 1H), 6.31 (t, J = 6.9 Hz, 1H), 6.02 (dt, J = 5.1, 16.1 Hz, 1H),
4.32 (d, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 4.05 (dd, J = 1.7, 5.1 Hz, 2H), 2.91-2.79 (m,
2H), 2.87 (s, 6H), 2.85 (s, 6H); 13C NMR (75 MHz): δ = 140.6, 140.1,
137.6, 137.4, 136.2, 134.8, 128.4, 16.1, 117.2, 115.5, 62.6, 58.4, 38.4,
38.3; IR (KBr, cm-1): 3360, 3136, 1476, 1420, 1386, 1276, 1180, 971;
HR-ESIMS (m/z): Calcd. for C16H25N6O6S2 [M+H]+ 461.1271, found 461.1277;
Calcd. for C16H24N6O6S2Na [M+Na]+ 483.1090, found 483.1098.
