$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Stille Reaction; General Method. A mixture of
triazole (1.0 mmol), vinylstannane (1.2 mmol), and PdCl2(MeCN)2 (0.06
mmol) in DMF (2 mL) was stirred overnight at 40 °C under an argon
atmosphere for 12 h. The mixture was poured into EtOAc (10 mL), filtered,
washed with sat. NH4Cl (3 × 10 mL) and brine (10 mL), dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude product was purified by
column chromatography (10% w/w anhyd K2CO3-silica gel, pentane-EtOAc,
100:0 to 60:40). 1-Benzyl-4-phenyl-5-(prop-1-en-2-yl)-1H-1,2,3-triazole
(5j). Orange solid; yield: 220 mg (80%). Reactant: Vinylstannane 4d. mp
63-64 °C. IR (neat): 2988, 2957, 2903, 1712, 1641, 1576, 1543, 1446,
1423, 1337, 1248, 1163, 1053, 976, 728, 691 cm-1. 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.72 (dd, J = 1.4, 1.0 Hz, 3 H), 5.18 (m, 1 H), 5.54 (s, 2
H), 5.56 (m, 1 H), 7.22 (m, 2 H), 7.28-7.35 (m, 4 H), 7.40 (m, 2 H), 7.84
(m, 2 H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 22.4, 51.9, 122.2, 126.5, 127.6,
127.9, 128.2, 128.7, 128.9, 131.2, 133.7, 134.7, 135.7, 143.6. HRMS
(ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for C18H18N3: 288.1495; found: 288.1488.
