$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 3-(3-allyl-4-methoxy-phenyl)-2-benzyloxy-5-bromo-pyridine
(9). A mixture of
2-benzyloxy-5-bromo-3-(3-iodo-4-methoxy-phenyl)-pyridine 3 (200 mg, 0.40
mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (233.49 mg, 0.20 mmol),
allyltributyltin (0.15 mL, 0.48 mmol) in benzene (5 mL) was degassed by
the stream of argon for 5 min. And then, the reaction mixture was stirred
for 3 h at 110 °C. The resulting mixture was concentrated in vacuo, and
the residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate =
50/1). Yield: (132 mg, 80%). 1H-NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.13 (d, 1H, J =
2.3 Hz), 7.70 (d, 1H, J = 2.8 Hz), 7.28-7.41 (m, 7H), 5.91-5.99 (m, 1H),
5.40 (s, 2H), 5.01-5.06 (m, 2H), 3.86 (s, 3H), 3.38 (d, 1H, J = 6.9 Hz).
13C-NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 159.0, 157.2, 145.4, 140.6, 137.3, 136.7,
130.9, 128.4(3), 128.2, 127.7(3), 127.4, 126.5, 116.1, 112.3, 110.3,
109.2, 68.1, 55.6, 34.3. HRMS(EI): m/z calcd for C22H20BrNO2 (M+H)+:
412.0736, obsd 412.0739.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, thermal, key step, Stille coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthetic approach to the chemical isostere of O-methyl honokiol
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cui, Minghua; Kim, Hak Sung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2012), 23(2), 311-313

