$DATUM 108-88-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Procedure A:3a A screw-cap vial was loaded
with the aryl bromide, aryl tri-n-butyltin, and then closed with a rubber
septum. After purging with argon, previously argon-bubbled toluene was
added via syringe to dissolve the materials. The system was bubbled with
argon for 30 min, followed by the addition of Pd(PPh3)4 under argon
atmosphere. High vacuum-argon bubbling cycles were performed 3 times and
then the vial was capped and covered from light. The reaction was heated
at 120 °C and allowed to react overnight. Once the reaction reached
completion, the mixture was allowed to cool to ambient temperature, and
the catalyst was removed by filtration over a silica pad using diethyl
ether as mobile phase. The organic phase was then washed with a saturated
solution of NaF and then water, dried over anhydrous MgSO4 and
concentrated using rotary evaporation. The crude product. All the
mixtures were purified by column chromatography. Prepared according to
the procedure A, using 2-tri-n-butylstannyl-thiophene (267 mg, 1.102
mmol), 1,4-dibromobenzene (130 mg, 0.551 mmol), and Pd(PPh3)4 (64 mg,
0.055 mmol). The product was obtained as off white solid after
purification by column chromatography using 10% DCM in hexanes as eluent
(107 mg, 80 % yield). m.p. 207-209 °C (lit7 210 °C) 1H NMR (300 MHz,
CDCl3): δ(ppm)= 7.61-7.64 (s, 4H); 7.33-7.35 (dd, 2H, J = 3.0, 1.0 Hz);
7.28-7.31 (d, 2H, J = 4.0, 1.0 Hz); 7.08-7.12 (dd, 2H, J = 4.0, 3.0 Hz).
Exact mass: 242.36, GC-MS: 242 (M.+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in the dark, Stille coupling
